# A theorem, proved by having no timeline.
#
# Claim: no 8-bit number has a cube equal to 2. (Check it yourself: the cubes mod 256 are
# 147 of the 256 values, and 2 is not one of them.)
#
# PARADOX has no "for all". It does not need one. Read the fixed point backwards:
#   consistent  <=>  a * a * a == 2   (any other message changes itself and dies)
# so the timelines ARE the counterexamples to the claim. A claim with no counterexample has
# no timeline at all, and "no timeline" is the proof. a -> a + 1 has no fixed point, so a
# counterexample cannot survive being sent.
bits 8
a = future(a)
if a * a * a != 2:
    a = a + 1
